1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,040
Have you ever said,

2
00:00:01,040 --> 00:00:03,060
"I'm so OCD," just because

3
00:00:03,060 --> 00:00:04,360
your desk is spotless?

4
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:05,980
Well, you're probably not.

5
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:07,460
OCD is not simply liking

6
00:00:07,460 --> 00:00:08,320
things clean,

7
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:10,080
tidy, or organized.

8
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:11,460
That could be more OCPD,

9
00:00:11,460 --> 00:00:12,310
by the way,

10
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:13,800
or obsessive-compulsive

11
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:15,200
personality disorder,

12
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:16,600
involving a long-standing

13
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:18,600
pattern of perfectionism,

14
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,020
order, and control.

15
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:21,640
But what actually happens in

16
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:23,120
the mind of someone with

17
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:24,040
OCD? It

18
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:25,180
all comes down,

19
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:26,480
uh, to two key elements.

20
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:27,940
First, the obsessions.

21
00:00:27,940 --> 00:00:29,820
Obsessions are distressing,

22
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:31,920
intrusive, and unwanted

23
00:00:31,920 --> 00:00:33,510
thoughts, fears,

24
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:34,610
images.

25
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:36,160
These obsessions can attach

26
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:38,350
themselves to almost anything,

27
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,020
religion, superstition.

28
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:41,440
They might involve the fear

29
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:42,200
of germs,

30
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:43,950
the fear of making mistakes,

31
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:44,940
or even the fear of

32
00:00:44,940 --> 00:00:46,060
harming someone.

33
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:46,240
And

34
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:46,970
you know,

35
00:00:46,980 --> 00:00:49,390
they are really frightening

36
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:51,240
because this thought goes

37
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:52,960
always against what the person

38
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:54,480
wants and values.

39
00:00:54,480 --> 00:00:55,540
This is what we call

40
00:00:55,540 --> 00:00:56,760
ego dystonic.

41
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:58,080
Now, the compulsions.

42
00:00:58,080 --> 00:00:59,740
They are the things a

43
00:00:59,740 --> 00:01:01,340
person feels driven to do

44
00:01:01,340 --> 00:01:03,400
to reduce the anxiety created

45
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:04,720
by the obsession.

46
00:01:04,720 --> 00:01:07,040
They are actions or mental

47
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:08,560
rituals used to reduce

48
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:11,060
anxiety. So compulsions can

49
00:01:11,060 --> 00:01:11,880
be visible,

50
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:13,520
like washing your hand again

51
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:15,280
and again or checking again

52
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:16,070
and again.

53
00:01:16,180 --> 00:01:17,260
They can also involve

54
00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:19,180
repeating actions according to

55
00:01:19,180 --> 00:01:19,850
a rule,

56
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:21,140
such as setting the TV

57
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:22,420
volume to an even number

58
00:01:22,420 --> 00:01:23,780
or clicking a pen three

59
00:01:23,780 --> 00:01:25,280
times before writing.

60
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:27,400
But not every compulsion can

61
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:28,000
be seen,

62
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:28,930
by the way,

63
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:29,820
because some of

64
00:01:29,820 --> 00:01:31,300
them are mental.

65
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:32,980
Some people count silently,

66
00:01:32,980 --> 00:01:34,880
replay conversations in their

67
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:35,630
minds,

68
00:01:35,740 --> 00:01:37,200
mentally review what they did,

69
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:38,600
or repeatedly ask for

70
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:39,720
reassurance. At

71
00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:41,540
work, someone might read the

72
00:01:41,540 --> 00:01:43,220
same email again and again

73
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:44,260
because they're afraid of

74
00:01:44,260 --> 00:01:45,900
making a serious mistake.

75
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:48,260
Another person might avoid any

76
00:01:48,260 --> 00:01:49,590
handshakes or

77
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:51,020
any physical contact.

78
00:01:51,020 --> 00:01:51,880
In fact,

79
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:53,120
the problem is not really

80
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:54,750
the thought itself,

81
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:56,860
but the anxiety it creates.

82
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:57,060
Let's

83
00:01:57,060 --> 00:01:58,040
give an example.

84
00:01:58,040 --> 00:01:59,800
A doubt triggers anxiety.

85
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:00,720
"Did I lock the door?"

86
00:02:00,720 --> 00:02:01,670
for example.

87
00:02:01,740 --> 00:02:03,320
So the person checks and

88
00:02:03,320 --> 00:02:05,230
feels better for a moment,

89
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:06,950
but the doubt returns.

90
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:08,880
This temporary relief keeps

91
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:10,240
the cycle going.

92
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:11,990
It's the OCD loop,

93
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:13,110
like a trap.

94
00:02:13,260 --> 00:02:15,200
The brain learns that acting

95
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:16,630
helps to feel better,

96
00:02:16,860 --> 00:02:18,450
even for a moment.

97
00:02:18,820 --> 00:02:19,960
So you will ask me,

98
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:21,440
why does OCD begin?

99
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:23,420
OCD doesn't actually have one

100
00:02:23,420 --> 00:02:24,260
single cause.

101
00:02:24,260 --> 00:02:25,700
Genetics, life stress,

102
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:27,380
life experiences may play a

103
00:02:27,380 --> 00:02:29,320
role. Stress can trigger or

104
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:30,640
worsen symptoms.

105
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:33,120
And research suggests that

106
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:35,000
differences in brain circuits,

107
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,460
uh, involving the cortex,

108
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:38,740
striatum, and the thalamus may

109
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:40,610
contribute to OCD.

110
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:42,700
These circuits help regulate

111
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:45,260
thoughts, detect problems and

112
00:02:45,260 --> 00:02:46,610
possible threats,

113
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:48,470
and control actions.

114
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:49,140
In OCD,

115
00:02:49,140 --> 00:02:50,940
this system may struggle to

116
00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:52,600
regulate signals as if a

117
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:54,960
false alarm keeps coming back.

118
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:55,160
So

119
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:56,160
how can we help?

120
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:58,120
Repeated reassurance such as,

121
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:58,900
"Don't worry,

122
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:00,760
it's fine," can reinforce the

123
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:02,050
OCD cycle.

124
00:03:02,160 --> 00:03:03,690
You can try instead,

125
00:03:03,800 --> 00:03:04,700
"I can see this is

126
00:03:04,700 --> 00:03:05,700
stressful for you.

127
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:07,380
What kind of support w-would

128
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:08,700
help right now?" We

129
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:10,640
can show compassion without

130
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:12,040
joining the ritual.

131
00:03:12,040 --> 00:03:13,900
The important message is that

132
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:15,790
OCD is treatable.

133
00:03:16,060 --> 00:03:18,360
ERP, or exposure and response

134
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:19,690
prevention therapy,

135
00:03:19,760 --> 00:03:22,110
helps people face their fears

136
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:23,520
and learn to tolerate

137
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:26,000
uncertainty without performing

138
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,110
compulsions.

139
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:29,040
Medication may also help

140
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:30,670
turn the volume down,

141
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:32,620
either on its own or

142
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:34,370
alongside a therapy.

143
00:03:34,620 --> 00:03:35,280
I would like you to

144
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:37,480
remember, OCD is much more

145
00:03:37,480 --> 00:03:38,500
than a preference for

146
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:39,960
neatness. It can be an

147
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:41,960
exhausting, invisible

148
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:42,580
struggle.

149
00:03:42,580 --> 00:03:44,460
So look beyond the visible,

150
00:03:44,460 --> 00:03:46,050
listen without judgment.

151
00:03:46,080 --> 00:03:47,210
Help create

152
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:48,450
a safer,

153
00:03:48,620 --> 00:03:50,770
more understanding workplace.
